		{
			"id": "link-24e621e6aff1b4a67fbc94cd450a46b3",
			"title": "Ask HN: Please restrict new accounts from posting",
			"link": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47300329",
			"contents": "<div class=\"Story_container\"><div class=\"Story_data\"><div class=\"Story_title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47300329\"><span>Ask HN: Please restrict new accounts from posting</span></a></div><div class=\"Story_meta\"><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47300329\">717 points</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=Oras\"><span>Oras</span></a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47300329\">6 days ago</a></span><span class=\"Story_separator\">|</span><span><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47300329\">508 comments</a></span><div class=\"Story_comment\"><span>I don’t know if I’m the only one, but I see lots of clearly AI generated posts recently in HN and mostly coming from new accounts (green), it is more noticeable in the Show HN section.<p>I wish the team can either restrict new accounts from posting or at least offer a default filtering where I can only see posts from accounts with certain criteria.</p><p>I don’t want to see HN becoming twitter, which is full of bots and noise, as this would be a really sad day.</p></span></div></div></div></div>",
			"retrieved": 1773053146666
		},
